Chapter: Camera

 The Camera effect is the right to look through the machine's camera. It
 is a bare marker here, the way Microphone is: capture and capture-raw
 are not declared in this chapter.

 They were, once, as effect operations with no handler, so a call died
 at emit with CDX2040. Unlike Location and Sensors, the hardware is
 real: codex-vm presents a UVC camera on root port 3 and delivers frames
 over isochronous transfers, and Works chapter GopUsbCam drives it. So
 capture is not a constant anywhere -- it is a frame off the wire.

 It is not in the foreword because reading the camera means driving an
 xHCI isochronous endpoint, and that is not a foreword concern. A
 chapter that wants the operations cites Works chapter CamCapture.

 We say:

Section: Definitions

  effect Camera where

